# pkg-config template for libfasm_capi (rust/fasm-capi), the C and C++
# (header-only, include/fasm/fasm.hpp) API of the fasm library.
#
# Substituted and installed by `make capi-install PREFIX=...` (see
# Makefile) into $(PREFIX)/lib/pkgconfig/fasm.pc: the three placeholders
# below (prefix path, version, private link libraries) are filled in from
# the install prefix, the crate version (rust/fasm-capi/Cargo.toml, i.e.
# the workspace root Cargo.toml) and the system libraries the static
# library needs (see rust/fasm-capi/tests/c/CMakeLists.txt's
# FASM_NATIVE_LIBS, from `cargo rustc -p fasm-capi -- --print
# native-static-libs`). Do not use the placeholder syntax anywhere else in
# this file (a plain `sed` substitutes every occurrence).
#
# `pkg-config --cflags --libs fasm` gives a dynamically linked build
# (`-lfasm_capi`, needing libfasm_capi.so at run time); link
# `libfasm_capi.a` directly (`-l:libfasm_capi.a $(pkg-config --libs.private
# fasm)`, or the CMake FASM_STATIC path in tests/c/CMakeLists.txt) for a
# static one. Both the C header and the C++ wrapper are reached through
# the same Cflags (-I${includedir}, giving <fasm/fasm.h> and
# <fasm/fasm.hpp>); the C++ wrapper needs no extra library (header only).

prefix=@PREFIX@
exec_prefix=${prefix}
includedir=${prefix}/include
libdir=${prefix}/lib

Name: fasm
Description: FASM (FPGA Assembly) parsing, model, output and merge library: C API (fasm/fasm.h) and header-only C++17 RAII wrapper (fasm/fasm.hpp)
Version: @VERSION@
Libs: -L${libdir} -lfasm_capi
Libs.private: @LIBS_PRIVATE@
Cflags: -I${includedir}
